/-!
# Pole divisor degree at most [F:K(x)]

Theorem statement: `AlgebraicCurve.Divisor.degree_le_finrank_adjoin_of_eq_max_neg_ord`
(`874c1f23-9139-58ac-bea5-69dda441aeaf`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `1164fb22-5272-5a31-bc88-20bd0fe26710`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $K$ and $F$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra satisfying `IsCurveOver K F`: every nonzero $f \in
F$ has a finitely supported divisor recording its orders, $D(v) = \operatorname{ord}_v f$ at every
place $v$, of degree $0$; every place has residue field finite over $K$; and $\Omega[F/K]$ is free
of rank one over $F$. Here a place $v$ of $F/K$ is a valuation subring of $F$ containing
$\operatorname{im}(K \to F)$, distinct from $F$ itself, which is a principal ideal ring,
$\operatorname{ord}_v$ is the associated normalised additive valuation, a divisor is a finitely
supported $\mathbb{Z}$-valued function on places, and $\deg D = \sum_v D(v)\deg v$. Assume in
addition that the Riemann–Roch space of the zero divisor, $\{f \in F : v(f) \le 1 \text{ for all }
v\}$, is finite-dimensional over $K$. Let $x \in F$ be transcendental over $K$ and assume $F$ is
finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $K(x)$ generated by $x$. Let $D$ be a divisor with
$D(v) = \max(0, -\operatorname{ord}_v x)$ for every place $v$, i.e. the pole divisor of $x$. Then
$\deg D \le [F : K(x)]$, the inequality taken in $\mathbb{Z}$.

This is one half of the classical identity $\deg (x)_\infty = [F:K(x)]$ for a one-variable function
field, the direction given by the fundamental inequality $\sum_{P \mid \infty} e_P f_P \le [F:K(x)]$
for the extensions of the infinite place of $K(x)$, and it requires no separability assumption. It
feeds into
[`AlgebraicCurve.Divisor.degree_eq_finrank_adjoin_of_eq_max_neg_ord`]
(thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.Divisor.degree_eq_finrank_adjoin_of_eq_max_neg_ord),
where the two inequalities are combined into the equality.

